title: "Orthonym"
abstract: >-
  Orthonym is a deterministic, rule-based engine that names a molecular
  structure (SMILES) following the IUPAC 2013 recommendations, aiming at the
  Preferred IUPAC Name; the same input always gives the same output. Before a
  name is returned, OPSIN reads it back and the structure it reads is compared
  with the input; a candidate that fails is withdrawn. A few names OPSIN cannot
  read in full (names from exact-match lists, a few name forms outside OPSIN's
  grammar, and stereodescriptors OPSIN cannot parse) are returned by the default
  tier without that full read-back and are marked in the provenance output. Every name carries a tier label that says
  whether the engine certifies it as the Preferred IUPAC Name.
